{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1042925-lightning-vs-vampires","id":1042925,"title":"Lightning vs. Vampires","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-02-03T07:15:59-08:00","id":1042925,"title":"Lightning vs. Vampires","content":"I'm running an Ordo vampire with the Coil of Zinitra, and I have Psychokinisis 5 for electricity. My GM has questioned the validity of my lightning doing lethal to vampires. I think it does, it's a supernatural ability(merit), normal electricity does bashing on it's own, but Psychokinisis specifically does lethal. It's far from mundane and I'm generating the lightning rather than pulling it from a mundane source. Anyone have any thoughts on the matter one way or the other?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12860-your3rdshadow","name":"Your3rdShadow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12860_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T07:31:07-08:00","id":1042937,"title":"","content":"I'd allow it to do lethal, but I can see the argument for bashing. It's a supernatural ability but it does damage by creating lightning, which isn't supernatural <i>per se</i>. Much like a weapon summoned by magic wouldn't do lethal to a vampire because the weapon itself isn't magical. But I would say it does lethal anyway for two reasons. First of all, electricity normally does bashing damage so it's clear there's something special about this lightning. And second of all, you paid experiences (or at least character creation dots) for the ability, so I would err towards allowing it to work as written whenever reasonable so as to not devalue that investment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T07:31:23-08:00","id":1042938,"title":"","content":"The way that electricity is manipulated (and conjured up with the five dot version) is definitely far from mundane, but the electricity itself should probably not be considered magical. The reason electricity does lethal from Psychokinesis is only because Psychokinesis is written to be a generic template Merit for different abilities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T07:35:47-08:00","id":1042939,"title":"","content":"First and foremost the Storyteller is always correct in his Chronicle, so everything I say is IMHO and should not be used to try and override the Storyteller. I would have it do Lethal as it is more magical the mundane. But then I am New to the Chronicles of Darkness so take what I say with a grain of salt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T07:44:28-08:00","id":1042943,"title":"","content":"Generally, damage is downgraded unless it specifically says otherwise. According to the book, even some supernatural attacks that do Aggravated are downgraded.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Kindred take only bashing damage from many sources that<br /> would normally cause lethal damage to humans. This <b>includes</b><br /> most non-supernatural weapons.<br /> <br /> Those few terrible things that cause aggravated wounds<br /> to mortals cause only lethal harm to vampires. This mostly<br /> includes terrible harm from chemicals, <b>certain supernatural<br /> punishment</b>, and the skills of utmost masters in certain fighting<br /> styles meant to maximize debilitating bodily harm. </div> </div> </div>Page 90, emphasis mine. &quot;Includes&quot; in this case suggesting that it isn't an exhaustive list regarding Lethal damage. Essentially, the same lack of working internal organs that downgrades other damage would have me downgrading electric damage, too. Supernatural or not, it's still electricity, and Supernatural damage as a whole doesn't get the blanket ability to bypass Vampiric damage reduction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T07:48:16-08:00","id":1042944,"title":"","content":"Basically, unless it's a bane or is otherwise designed to not be downgraded by vampires (such as the Protean 4 claws) it should be downgraded.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T07:55:05-08:00","id":1042947,"title":"","content":"Going to go with the general flow here - it's not supernatural lightning, just supernaturally manipulated/created lightning. It should do Bashing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T08:06:42-08:00","id":1042952,"title":"","content":"In as much as intent matters, here'a what David has said about it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/122291-uratha-teeth-and-claws?p=125207#post125207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At the time I wrote that particular remark, I only knew of one GMC compliant supernatural power that did aggravated damage (a Demon power), and felt it should be downgraded.<br /> <br /> Since at the time, we were really only thinking of Vampire for the most part, it does require a little more consideration if you want to look at crossover games and such.<br /> <br /> My personal rules of thumb are basically:<br /> <br /> If it'd do aggravated to a human, it does lethal to a vampire.<br /> If it'd do lethal to a human, it does bashing to a vampire.<br /> If it's a direct damage power in a Vampire book, it does the damage suggested since we're referencing vampires primarily in that book.<br /> If the power makes a mundane weapon or cause of harm, downgrade it. Protean 2 is a good example.<br /> If the power makes a weapon, and we say it does X to vampires, it does X to vampires. Protean 4 is a good example.<br /> If someone in my games paid Experience for something to hurt vampires, it should hurt them. A Fighting Style that does aggravated should probably do aggravated, because of the investment involved.</div> </div> </div> </div>So yeah. Like I said, I'd allow it to do lethal to honor the experience investment in the power, and because it's already doing different damage than electricity normally does, which clearly indicates that it is supernaturally empowered in some way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 02-03-2017, 11:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T08:13:57-08:00","id":1042956,"title":"","content":"And that is where I was coming from that it is more magic the Mundane.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T10:46:00-08:00","id":1043032,"title":"","content":"Vampires are not inherently more vulnerable to magic than to mundane sources of injury, because magic isn't just one thing, or even a large set of loosely-related things.<br /> <br /> That said, between the experience investment in the power and the fact that one of the dangers of lightning is getting burned, I'd let it do lethal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":2,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","user":"Rose Bailey","date":". 02-03-2017, 04:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T12:46:13-08:00","id":1043102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1042925-lightning-vs-vampires?p=1043032#post1043032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampires are not inherently more vulnerable to magic than mundane sources of injury, because magic isn't just one thing, or even a large set of loosely-related things.<br /> <br /> That said, between the experience investment in the power and the fact that one of the dangers of lightning is getting burned, I'd let it do lethal.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd let it do lethal, for the reasons Rose quoted. Also because a) lightning is much more powerful and more damaging to non-living objects than other sources of electrical damage b) scientifically speaking, a sizable part of the damage lightning causes is high-intensity burning c) mystically speaking, lightning is close to fire in elemental affinities. In sum, lightning is too powerful and close to fire to do bashing damage to vampires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 02-03-2017, 06:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T13:40:55-08:00","id":1043128,"title":"","content":"I'd go with bashing as otherwise I would feel that any Spirt with the Blast Numina should do lethal too but you do have a quote from the woman who made the book that says lethal. Show your ST the post (and this whole thread) and accept his judgment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T14:45:09-08:00","id":1043155,"title":"","content":"We have reached an Agreement, thank you all for the well reasoned responses and your interest. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12860-your3rdshadow","name":"Your3rdShadow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12860_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T14:55:31-08:00","id":1043162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irioth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1042925-lightning-vs-vampires?p=1043102#post1043102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">scientifically speaking, a sizable part of the damage lightning causes is high-intensity burning c) mystically speaking, lightning is close to fire in elemental affinities.</div> </div> </div> </div>Try telling that to a Promethean though <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T14:58:07-08:00","id":1043164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1042925-lightning-vs-vampires?p=1043032#post1043032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampires are not inherently more vulnerable to magic than to mundane sources of injury, because magic isn't just one thing, or even a large set of loosely-related things.<br /> <br /> That said, between the experience investment in the power and the fact that one of the dangers of lightning is getting burned, I'd let it do lethal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oooh, I just noticed your a devloper!! Senpai Noticed me!!!!!!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12860-your3rdshadow","name":"Your3rdShadow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12860_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T18:37:37-08:00","id":1043296,"title":"","content":"As an electrician, I always thought it would make sense for high power electrical damage to have a small chance of setting the victim's clothes/hair on fire, but it's never come up in a game of mine.<br /> Also the primary damage from electricity is indeed burning, it just burns from the inside out instead of outside in like a fire. Your insides of course don't catch fire because of all the moisture and lack of oxygen, and vamps bane is Fire itself, not just heat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11661,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","user":"Rathamus","date":". 02-03-2017, 09:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T03:25:49-08:00","id":1043445,"title":"","content":"I've also worked with electricity and can verify Rathamus. Now, this thread is about electricity that someone paid XP for so it shouldn't be downgraded according to the guidelines posted, but electricity in general should not be more dangerous to vampires than humans. Vampires shouldn't really care about nerve damage or bodily fluids literally boiling since they don't actually use those things. Unless they catch fire (which can happen if someone gets continuously struck by an arc of electricity (which usually requires 1000+ Volt) or gets stuck for a longer time while wearing metallic jewelry close to the path the electricity takes through the body) the body's structural integrity is basically unchanged for the purpose of how vampires animates their bodies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T04:43:11-08:00","id":1043470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1042925-lightning-vs-vampires?p=1043445#post1043445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampires shouldn't really care about nerve damage or bodily fluids literally boiling since they don't actually use those things.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with most everything you said save what I quoted above. Vitae is a bodily fluid and I am fairly certain that they care if that gets burned away.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T04:48:00-08:00","id":1043474,"title":"","content":"Vitae is not in itself a bodily fluid, but it's stored in one. However, losing blood/Vitae from damage (as per the Kindred Dueling Fighting Style) does not deal damage to a vampire. Instead that vampire simply loses their Vitae. I'm not sure how that would be represented by the game in case of electrical damage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T05:01:05-08:00","id":1043479,"title":"","content":"You can get burned by ice/extreme cold tempatures, from chemicals, and boiling water as well as from electricity and fire. I'm really not convinced that &quot;getting burns&quot; is a good argument for lethal damage in this case. As another said, extreme heat is not a bane. Now, if clothes caught fire, that'd be one thing, but that's not what we're discussing here, and I don't think I'd allow that with electrokinesis from a vampire, since I'm also opposed to vampires with pyrokinesis. No evoking anything approaching banes as powers.<br /> <br /> As for the argument that the player sunk XP into a power? Perhaps that would be true if there wasn't more to the ability than shooting electricity in combat. But you can power electronics, arguably control computers and machines to an extent, shape electricity in artistic ways, increase or decrease the intensity of it, manifest it from nothing, and more. Attacking is only one of <i>sixth </i>of the abilities you get with psychokinesis at best. In theory, I think you can even use electricity to put out fires by ionizing the oxygen in the air, though I'd probably require an exceptional success for that.<br /> <br /> Now, if it was an ability where dealing combat damage was its -only- ability, then yeah, I could see that argument. Or even half of the things you can do. If violence is somehow the purpose of the ability, then I would agree with &quot;spent xp = lethal.&quot; But I can't agree with that argument when psychokinesis does so much. If &quot;spent xp&quot; was the deciding factor, then Protean 2 claws would be dealing lethal as well. They don't. Should someone who spent XP to buy Martial Arts 4 be able to deal lethal to vampires? I'm not convinced that should either, despite being an ability that primarily revolves around dealing damage.<br /> <br /> There's some flexibility in here depending on the game, and I'm not a fan of allowing it. It just doesn't feel thematically appropriate to me, and that's not the kind of story I would want to tell. <br /> <br /> Now, if the OP bought the power with the expectation of dealing lethal, and only intends on doing lethal, and there was no discussion on the matter beforehand, I would allow, as an ST, for the player to refund the ability for something more relevant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 02-04-2017, 08:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T13:46:26-08:00","id":1043710,"title":"","content":"Do TF:V still get their experimental weapons as merits? If so does that mean their bullets do lethal?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-05T07:55:59-08:00","id":1043984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1042925-lightning-vs-vampires?p=1043479#post1043479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can get burned by ice/extreme cold tempatures, from chemicals, and boiling water as well as from electricity and fire. I'm really not convinced that &quot;getting burns&quot; is a good argument for lethal damage in this case. As another said, extreme heat is not a bane. Now, if clothes caught fire, that'd be one thing, but that's not what we're discussing here, and I don't think I'd allow that with electrokinesis from a vampire, since I'm also opposed to vampires with pyrokinesis. No evoking anything approaching banes as powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>The issue here is whether the source of burning is of the kind that does substantial damage to inanimate matter and causes significant loss of substance, not just living tissue or disruption of biological functions that may be inactive or unnecessary in vampires. Lightning does, just like strong acids/bases, and because of this it is different from other sources of electrical damage (something I think Rathamus and Tessie may be not mindful enough of), or for that matter poisons, extreme cold, extreme heat, or boiling water. So IMO it is entirely justified and fitting lightning and certain chemicals do lethal damage to vampires. I also don't see any problem with vampires having pyrokinesis, since vampires develop various kinds of powers that help them control, mitigate, or otherwise deal with their banes all the time. You may notice the power that allows vampires to have psychokinesis in the first place belongs to the covenant that made its mission to overcome the limitations of Kindred existence, so it is an entirely appropriate extension of its purview. Pyrokinesis as bestowed by the Coil of Zirnitra is just another weapon in the Ordo Dracul's arsenal for its anti-banes and trans-vampiric quest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 02-05-2017, 12:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-05T09:28:51-08:00","id":1044022,"title":"","content":"Blood Sorcery explicitly can't create Banes.<br /> <br /> The Mystery of the Ascendant, which is an entire Mystery dealing specifically with the Banes of Fire and Sunlight, cannot grant power over either one.<br /> <br /> Why does a Mystery that is entirely unrelated to Banes give more power over Banes than the one that is entirely about them?<br /> <br /> Plus it just seems really against theme for a vampire to be slinging around and controlling a substance that is supposed to symbolically and literally destroy them. And I'm not even sure how you'd learn it with the whole Frenzy issue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-05T10:02:43-08:00","id":1044045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1042925-lightning-vs-vampires?p=1044022#post1044022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Blood Sorcery explicitly can't create Banes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Bane manipulation is the purview of the Coils, not Blood Sorcery. And the Coil of Zirnitra does not directly manipulate fire: it unlocks access to a psychic power that allows to create and control fire, electricity, or cold (or even two or three elements at once if you buy the Psychokinesis Merit multiple times).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Mystery of the Ascendant, which is an entire Mystery dealing specifically with the Banes of Fire and Sunlight, cannot grant power over either one. </div> </div> </div>The Coil of the Ascendant does something different: it provides increased resistance to fire and sunlight, and makes the vampire more lifelike. Pyrokinesis as bestowed by the Coil of Zirnitra and the Psychokinesis Merit allows the vampire to push fire away from oneself or snuff it out (among other things). One is similar to wearing fire-resistant body armor all the time. The other is akin to carrying a fire extinguisher (with a charge equivalent to one's Willpower) all the time. They are different and complementary enough in their approach they can easily co-exist.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Plus it just seems really against theme for a vampire to be slinging around and controlling a substance that is supposed to symbolically and literally destroy them. </div> </div> </div>Vampires are entirely able to sling around and control fire by mundane means (barring frenzy issues) - grab a flamethrower and/or an extinguisher - so I'm unable to see any theme issues here. Besides, the main theme of the Coils includes overcoming Kindred limitations and allowing vampires to 'cheat' with banes, frenzy, humanity, and other foibles, so it overrides any such concerns.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And I'm not even sure how you'd learn it with the whole Frenzy issue. </div> </div> </div>The Coil of the Ascendant can help a lot here, and so do high Willpower and/or the Coil of the Wyrm. Pretty much any trick that helps vampires control frenzies may be the solution. I expect most vampires that are interested in getting pyrokinesis develop high Resolve + Composure, the Coil of the Ascendant, and/or the Coil of the Wyrm in parallel to the Coil of Zirnitra and Psychokinesis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 02-05-2017, 04:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-05T15:05:25-08:00","id":1044204,"title":"","content":"Why are we talking about science in front of a walking corpse, again?<br /> <br /> The Bane of Fire is a mystical quality, so I highly doubt the physical definitions of burning matter here. Does it register symbolically as fire? No? Then no bane treatment.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Coils are about transcending the vampiric condition, so an excuse could be made for messing with fire, but let's remember that it's an ongoing process whose completion is a narrative event rather than a mere spend-more-Experiences thing, and an arduous and consuming process that most vampires can't bother to develop more than one. Added with how Coils like Zirnitra are obscure and rare even by Ordo standards, and the hypothetical vampire who can control fire willy-nilly by mastering multiple Mysteries seem more like a white room thing only player characters have the luxury to indulge in, rather than something that could commonly exist in the background.<br /> <br /> Even still, how the Admonitoria can't access fire and sunlight with Contracts, an entirely out-of-context power for vampires that are even more displaced from vampiric nature than the Coils, seem to lean in favor of &quot;powers derived from the vampiric condition can't manipulate its banes&quot; interpretation. The fact that a clever (and calm) vampire can pick up a torch or a flamethrower is unrelated, since we're talking about supernatural powers derived from within here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-05T16:33:29-08:00","id":1044266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1042925-lightning-vs-vampires?p=1044204#post1044204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why are we talking about science in front of a walking corpse, again?<br /> <br /> The Bane of Fire is a mystical quality, so I highly doubt the physical definitions of burning matter here. Does it register symbolically as fire? No? Then no bane treatment.</div> </div> </div> </div>We are not discussing whether lightning should deal aggravated or not. Nobody argues about it being a bane. The issue is lightning is different in power and intensity from other electrical damage that mostly harms the body by messing with biological functions that are irrelevant for vampires. It can easily melt or break inanimate matter, so it should be treated like lethal damage for a walking corpse that has no special mystical resistance or vulnerability to electricity. If magic is slient on the issue, science is the next best guide.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Coils are about transcending the vampiric condition, so an excuse could be made for messing with fire, but let's remember that it's an ongoing process whose completion is a narrative event rather than a mere spend-more-Experiences thing, and an arduous and consuming process that most vampires can't bother to develop more than one. Added with how Coils like Zirnitra are obscure and rare even by Ordo standards, and the hypothetical vampire who can control fire willy-nilly by mastering multiple Mysteries seem more like a white room thing only player characters have the luxury to indulge in, rather than something that could commonly exist in the background. </div> </div> </div>The rarity of a power has no relevance to its features or effectiveness, and I disagree most experienced Ordo vampires never bother developing more than one Mystery. Nobody said Pyrokinesis-yielding vampires are a common occurence, just that some characters can develop it by existing rules with enough effort and dedication.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Even still, how the Admonitoria can't access fire and sunlight with Contracts, an entirely out-of-context power for vampires that are even more displaced from vampiric nature than the Coils, seem to lean in favor of &quot;powers derived from the vampiric condition can't manipulate its banes&quot; interpretation. The fact that a clever (and calm) vampire can pick up a torch or a flamethrower is unrelated, since we're talking about supernatural powers derived from within here. </div> </div> </div>The Coil of Zirnitra does not directly manipulate Banes. It unlocks access to different kinds of mystical powers from other templates, unrelated to the vampiric conditions, that can do so. Notice the difference. You may also notice the RAW of the Mystery includes no prohibition of buying pyrokinesis or other supernatural powers (e.g. Forces spells) that manipulate Banes, unlike Blood Sorcery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 02-05-2017, 07:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-05T17:13:41-08:00","id":1044285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irioth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1042925-lightning-vs-vampires?p=1044266#post1044266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> We are not discussing whether lightning should deal aggravated or not. Nobody argues about it being a bane. The issue is lightning is different in power and intensity from other electrical damage that mostly harms the body by messing with biological functions that are irrelevant for vampires. It can easily melt or break inanimate matter, so it should be treated like lethal damage for a walking corpse that has no special mystical resistance or vulnerability to electricity. If magic is slient on the issue, science is the next best guide.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair point. But do Structure damage track bashing-lethal-aggravated differently like living and undead flesh do? Both living and undead creatures take damage from electicity by suffering a bucket load of bashing damage that wraps to lethal. Lightning probably inflicts more than a dozen levels of bashing damage in one turn, enough to count as lethal damage for everybody. Ruling that lightning damages vampires differently seems like an unnecessary complication, when we can just use the rules for electricity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The rarity of a power has no relevance to its features or effectiveness, and I disagree most experienced Ordo vampires never bother developing more than one Mystery. </div> </div> </div>Lost me here, so I'll just rephrase what I was trying to say, before trying to answer to something I can't quite grasp clearly.<br /> <br /> What I meant was that the complete attainment of whatever the Coil is supposed to grant to the vampire, to the point of truly transcending the vampiric condition, is something you'll see rarely in games, much like Ascension-by-Legacy in Mage games. I think buying powers that grant mastery over vampiric banes fall into that category, because it is the capstone of &quot;using foreign powers to augment the vampiric condition&quot; that the Coil of Zirnitra embodies.<br /> <br /> And I still think developing multiple Mysteries is something that only player characters, already inclined towards hyper-accelerated growth, are entitled to.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Nobody said Pyrokinesis-yielding vampires are a common occurence, just that some characters can develop it by existing rules with enough effort and dedication. </div> </div> </div>Yes, but so are all those crazy white room builds about the hypothetical vampire who can bash a werewolf in melee. Which I find awkward, but I guess this is a matter of personal taste.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Coil of Zirnitra does not directly manipulate Banes. It unlocks access to different kinds of mystical powers from other templates, unrelated to the vampiric conditions, that can do so. Notice the difference. You may also notice the RAW of the Mystery includes no prohibition of buying pyrokinesis or other supernatural powers (e.g. Forces spells) that manipulate Banes, unlike Blood Sorcery. </div> </div> </div>The Admonitoria condition also unlocks access to a different kind of mystical power from another template, unrelated to the vampiric condition, which still can't manipulate fire and sunlight and functional stakes.<br /> <br /> And yes, the RAW includes no prohibition. Which is sad, because it means the rules are choking the themes instead of embellishing it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-05T18:29:13-08:00","id":1044312,"title":"","content":"I'm assuming the electricity is of the correct voltage to cause severe electric shock hence the lethal damage. That means the body is effectively being turned into a heating coil, think electric heater. There would be little to no burning involved, perhaps more in the case of a vampire body. In fact, a vampire's body being dead could indicate a reason why it might still should be lethal, or not. Either way, direct damage is a resistance roll and I think supernatural tolerance should be included. That would make it less effective on vampires. I don't know about the indirect damage.<br /> <br /> The guy that wrote the Coil actually has written that vampires shouldn't have pyrokinesis, not psychokinesis though. I think it might be in Hurt Locker. I don't remember now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-05T19:40:45-08:00","id":1044332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1042925-lightning-vs-vampires?p=1044285#post1044285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I meant was that the complete attainment of whatever the Coil is supposed to grant to the vampire, to the point of truly transcending the vampiric condition, is something you'll see rarely in games, much like Ascension-by-Legacy in Mage games. I think buying powers that grant mastery over vampiric banes fall into that category, because it is the capstone of &quot;using foreign powers to augment the vampiric condition&quot; that the Coil of Zirnitra embodies.<br /> <br /> And I still think developing multiple Mysteries is something that only player characters, already inclined towards hyper-accelerated growth, are entitled to.</div> </div> </div> </div>It seems we come to this discussion from widely diverging perspectives. As I see it, developing multiple Mysteries is (or should be) something fairly common in the Ordo Dracul, more or less as developing a few out-of-clan Disciplines in the general vampire population. Narrow and stereotype niche specializations are stifling and boring, and moreso their widespread prevalence in the general supernatural population.<br /> <br /> And to develop one or more Mysteries to the fullest degree of canon abilities included in the books does not really qualify for true transcendence of the vampiric condition. It brings you a good deal down the road but not really there. More or less the same way to achieve mastery in one or more Arcana does not make you an Archmage. Neither the abilities Pyrokinesis provides mean complete mastery of the fire bane: they essentially allow to duplicate the effects of mundane equipment w/o the issues of equipment. Damn useful but nothing transcendent or wholly beyond the power of other vampiric abilities. That kind of 'vampire demigod' power is something all canon Mysteries hint to, but do not really provide, and so far something that can only explored by houserules in individual chronicles. We shall see if anything changes in this regard once the elders sourcebook gets published.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yes, but so are all those crazy white room builds about the hypothetical vampire who can bash a werewolf in melee. Which I find awkward, but I guess this is a matter of personal taste. </div> </div> </div>Personal taste indeed. I find to cling to endless variations of the default splat archetypes and character builds suggested by the games is stifling and boring, especially for experienced or creative players. The world and humanity are vast and diverse, and so are the supernatural populations, therefore there is room for nearly any buildable character concept to exist if the player cares to build it that way, provided there is any barely decent justification for its existence. I find character-background justifications for say a few supernaturals who dedicated themselves to master pretty much every power available to their splat or build themselves into fighting machines that can bash combat-specialized splats in melee trivially easy to come by, even if they defy default niche specializations and stereotypes of a splat.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And yes, the RAW includes no prohibition. Which is sad, because it means the rules are choking the themes instead of embellishing it. </div> </div> </div>If the Coil of Zirnitra were not a Coil but another kind of vampiric power, or the Coils of the Ascendant, the Wyrm, and Ziva did not exist, I might perhaps agree. But since it is part of the Ordo's arsenal and these powers exist (their rarity being irrelevant in this context), I find it fulfills the Ordo's main theme nicely, and the trans-vampiric theme of the Ordo overrides and nullifies any other similar concerns you might see here. I think the game gets much better for the Ordo Dracul and its specialty tricks existing, and their big fat bird being flipped to whatever agent or force created the limitations of the vampiric condition. Admittedly this perspective comes from a transhumanist guy that finds horror entirely boring and incomprehensible, and can only play the WoD as a mix of action-adventure, urban fantasy, intrigue, soap-opera, and mystery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 02-06-2017, 09:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-05T19:43:37-08:00","id":1044334,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irioth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1042925-lightning-vs-vampires?p=1043984#post1043984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The issue here is whether the source of burning is of the kind that does substantial damage to inanimate matter and causes significant loss of substance, not just living tissue or disruption of biological functions that may be inactive or unnecessary in vampires. Lightning does, just like strong acids/bases, and because of this it is different from other sources of electrical damage (something I think Rathamus and Tessie may be not mindful enough of), or for that matter poisons, extreme cold, extreme heat, or boiling water. So IMO it is entirely justified and fitting lightning and certain chemicals do lethal damage to vampires. I also don't see any problem with vampires having pyrokinesis, since vampires develop various kinds of powers that help them control, mitigate, or otherwise deal with their banes all the time. You may notice the power that allows vampires to have psychokinesis in the first place belongs to the covenant that made its mission to overcome the limitations of Kindred existence, so it is an entirely appropriate extension of its purview. Pyrokinesis as bestowed by the Coil of Zirnitra is just another weapon in the Ordo Dracul's arsenal for its anti-banes and trans-vampiric quest.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, lightning carries mostly the same risks of other types of high voltage electrical contact. The only major difference is that the heat build up is a lot quicker and can lead to an almost explosive expansion of the air in the lungs, but damages to nerves, blood vessels and the heart is definitely more dangerous for humans. While lightning maybe should deal lethal instead of bashing, vampires should still downgrade it to bashing since the damages for a vampire should still be less noticable than most weapons.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1042925-lightning-vs-vampires?p=1044312#post1044312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The guy that wrote the Coil actually has written that vampires shouldn't have pyrokinesis, not psychokinesis though. I think it might be in Hurt Locker. I don't remember now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pyrokinesis is just a flavour name for Psychokinesis from the core book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-05T19:58:36-08:00","id":1044341,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1042925-lightning-vs-vampires?p=1044312#post1044312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The guy that wrote the Coil actually has written that vampires shouldn't have pyrokinesis, not psychokinesis though. I think it might be in Hurt Locker. I don't remember now.</div> </div> </div> </div>No such prohibition got added to the book so far that I know of. The book is still getting errata'ed, and IIRC the new Coils already got a few significant clarifications and adjustments between open development and the advance version. Let's wait and see if any such hypothetical prohibition gets added to the final version. Otherwise, I'm not going to find hearsay about what a writer might have posted in some forum authoritative enough to heed an interpretation I dislike.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 02-05-2017, 11:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-05T20:23:16-08:00","id":1044352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1042925-lightning-vs-vampires?p=1044334#post1044334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually, lightning carries mostly the same risks of other types of high voltage electrical contact. The only major difference is that the heat build up is a lot quicker and can lead to an almost explosive expansion of the air in the lungs, but damages to nerves, blood vessels and the heart is definitely more dangerous for humans. While lightning maybe should deal lethal instead of bashing, vampires should still downgrade it to bashing since the damages for a vampire should still be less noticable than most weapons.</div> </div> </div> </div>No matter what, I find the very notion of a lightning-strike being less serious than a sword-strike to a walking corpse silly and unplausible, unless the latter means decapitation or at least a cut limb. Extra biological damage caused by electricity to living creatures is irrelevant here. The issue is the sheer, vast amount of damaging energy released by a lightning.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 02-06-2017, 03:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-06T03:35:31-08:00","id":1044429,"title":"","content":"Which is not that great, tbh. Sure, you're looking at long term injuries and a whooping 10% mortality rate, but it's not an order of magnitude worse than being shot with a gun. In game terms lightning should simply have a larger damage mod than a gun. Not aggravated damage to humans or unprecedentedly ignore the downgrading of vampires.<br /> <br /> That's talking about actual lightning. When it comes to Psychokinesis damage should be represented by how powerful the user's control of the element is, and I think it works fine as it is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 02-06-2017, 06:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-06T04:28:08-08:00","id":1044438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irioth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1042925-lightning-vs-vampires?p=1043984#post1043984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The issue here is whether the source of burning is of the kind that does substantial damage to inanimate matter and causes significant loss of substance, not just living tissue or disruption of biological functions that may be inactive or unnecessary in vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div> No, it is not. If we were dealing lethal-via-loss-of-substance, the power would be dealing aggravated to mortals. It does not. Which means that, if lightning is dealing lethal to vampires without upgrading the damage to mortals, it has to be because its somehow related to banes or because its an xp-based ability and the ST is generous.<br /> <br /> Lightning, even if it causes burns, is unrelated to a vampiric bane. Its not fire, its not sunlight, its not the jaws of a predator beast, nor is it a Humanity-based bane. Heat is not the same thing as fire, so even if lightning heated up the insides of a vampire and cooked them, its still not a bane.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Lightning does, just like strong acids/bases, </div> </div> </div> As far as I'm aware, acid does bashing to vampires as well, despite causing burns. The main reason why the developers suggested the power deal lightning is because &quot;player invested XP in it.&quot; You don't invest xp in vials of acid. There's no justification for acid causing lethal to vampires unless you're ruling it causes aggravated to mortals as well. In the OPs case, we're talking about dealing lethal to both mortals and vampires, so even if we do claim acid = aggravated to morals, this is unrelated to the discussion at hand.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I also don't see any problem with vampires having pyrokinesis, since vampires develop various kinds of powers that help them control, mitigate, or otherwise deal with their banes all the time. </div> </div> </div> No, they don't. Writers and developers have gone on to say that vampires actually shouldn't be able to control any kind of banes, including the writer who made Zirnitra. Its a statement I agree with and run with in my games. Mitigate, yes. Control / manipulate / deal with beyond weakening the damage it causes? Nope.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You may notice the power that allows vampires to have psychokinesis in the first place belongs to the covenant that made its mission to overcome the limitations of Kindred existence, so it is an entirely appropriate extension of its purview. </div> </div> </div> Except you're forgetting the small bit that Zirnitra doesn't necessarily allow pyrokinesis. STs have full control over what they decide is or is not appropriate and can ban mortal-supernatural merits at will. Its written right in the Coil. Given what I said above, pyrokinesis is out for my games. A vampire using lightning to create fire is also out.<br /> <br /> You want to run with fire powers in your game, more power to you. However, it is far from cannon. You cannot use it as an argument.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irioth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1042925-lightning-vs-vampires?p=1044352#post1044352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No matter what, I find the very notion of a lightning-strike being less serious than a sword-strike to a walking corpse silly and unplausible, unless the latter means decapitation or at least a cut limb. Extra biological damage caused by electricity to living creatures is irrelevant here. The issue is the sheer, vast amount of damaging energy released by a lightning.</div> </div> </div> </div> And so we get to the heart of the matter.<br /> <br /> Who said that lightning is less serious than a sword strike? They're both dealing bashing damage, and lightning will do more bashing damage on average than a sword. The only time swords do lethal is through Kindred Dueling, which specifically does do things like take out entire chunks of flesh.<br /> <br /> And I'm going to have to bring up the extra biological damage to living creatures, because it is relevant. Why should a vampire who doesn't take that extra biological damage still suffer the same amount of lethal damage as a mortal from lightning? That makes no sense. Humans are having their internal organs fried, which is kind of important to their survival. Vampires don't care if their internal organs are cooked or not. They're mostly dead weight, no pun intended. A vampire and a human will both have their insides equally fried from lightning.<br /> <br /> Should the vampire care about fried organs as much as the mortal? My answer is a resounding &quot;no.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 02-06-2017, 07:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-06T04:33:59-08:00","id":1044440,"title":"","content":"In your games run it as you see fit, we have a official ruling from the devs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-06T05:00:10-08:00","id":1044443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1042925-lightning-vs-vampires?p=1044440#post1044440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In your games run it as you see fit, we have a official ruling from the devs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nooooo.... we have how the writers would run things in their personal games. It is not an official ruling. There is a difference. &quot;I'd allow it&quot; does not equal &quot;this is the rule.&quot; <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-06T05:17:02-08:00","id":1044448,"title":"","content":"Jus run it how you want, just remember that real world physics has no baring on fantacy/comic book physics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-06T05:52:34-08:00","id":1044455,"title":"","content":"BTW the ruling that I was referin to was mentioned in post 8 by <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar269_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"269\" data-vbnamecard=\"269\">Charlaquin</a> as she was quoting Dave's list. Look as item 3 &quot;If it's a direct damage power in a Vampire book, it does the damage suggested since we're referencing vampires primarily in that book.&quot; That doesn\u2019t look like his opinion. I could be wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-06T06:20:08-08:00","id":1044468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1042925-lightning-vs-vampires?p=1044455#post1044455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">BTW the ruling that I was referin to was mentioned in post 8 by <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar269_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"269\" data-vbnamecard=\"269\">Charlaquin</a> as she was quoting Dave's list. Look as item 3 &quot;If it's a direct damage power in a Vampire book, it does the damage suggested since we're referencing vampires primarily in that book.&quot; That doesn\u2019t look like his opinion. I could be wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>Psychokinesis is in the God Machine Chronicles, which is the standard book for human characters, not Blood and Smoke, which is the standard book for vampire characters. And it's still just an opinion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-06T08:10:40-08:00","id":1044517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1042925-lightning-vs-vampires?p=1044312#post1044312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...<br /> <br /> The guy that wrote the Coil actually has written that vampires shouldn't have pyrokinesis, not psychokinesis though. I think it might be in Hurt Locker. I don't remember now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you reference where it is said that Vampires can't have Pyrokinesis?<br /> <br /> Because Hurt Locker actually has these things to say on the question of Pyrokinesis and Coils (the sidebar says Ziva, but should be Zirnitra) the &quot;But What If We Want Them Anyway?&quot; Sidebar is there to say that not only it is possible, it could be awesome (I have a pyrokinetic vamp, and yes I think he is awesome).<br /> <br /> &quot;As with anything, you have to consider its impact in your game. Adding a pyrokinetic character to your Vampire: The Requiem game might be a little difficult. Then again, it might be awesome.&quot;<br /> <br /> The Coil of the Ascendant is already transcendant of fire. Vampires with &quot;Peace with the Flame&quot; have less to fear from fire than mortals.<br /> <br /> Starting from &quot;Embolden Potential&quot; vampires start being arguably better at &quot;Mortal Supernatural Merits&quot; than mortals, and definitely better once past that.<br /> <br /> There is no RAW or RAI hard limits concerning Banes, Powers and how they interact. The only right answer here is that there is no one answer.<br /> <br /> So, it seems to be the contrary of what you are suggesting.<br /> <br /> On Lightning, Vampires and Damage;<br /> \u200b<br /> &quot;Only Flesh&quot; Sidebar:<br /> <br /> ...In short, if you plan to use these for the various supernatural game lines, just consider what effects they\u2019ll<br /> have on your narrative. <u><i><b>Modify them, or selectively allow them as you see fit.</b></i></u><br /> <br /> &quot;A Note on Monsters&quot; Sidebar:<br /> <br /> <i><u><b>There\u2019s no hard rule here.</b></u></i><br /> However, as a rule of thumb, if the Merit or effect has a per-use cost to the character, or adds a degree of<br /> risk (for example, if the character must sacrifice her Defense or spend Willpower), you should favor allowing<br /> the effect to cause its stated damage.<br /> <br /> (Which is the best argument Electrokinesis causing lethal, as the attacks cost Willpower. But it's still just an option, there is no right answer)<br /> <br /> In general, in games I get to decide, Electrokinesis will do bashing to vampires because vampires have a &quot;power&quot; to downgrade such damage. I dislike the whole &quot;if paid exp/willpower/defense&quot; things because it would be a shitfest argument if both the attacker and the target are PCs, and cause problematic extrapolations and expectations. So I just let the powers stand as the are written and avoid all that.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-06T10:03:13-08:00","id":1044579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1042925-lightning-vs-vampires?p=1044455#post1044455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">BTW the ruling that I was referin to was mentioned in post 8 by <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> as she was quoting Dave's list. Look as item 3 &amp;quot;If it's a direct damage power in a Vampire book, it does the damage suggested since we're referencing vampires primarily in that book.&amp;quot; That doesn\u2019t look like his opinion. I could be wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>Psychokinesis isn't actually in a vampire book. Also, I wouldn't call David's list an official ruling. Good advice, yes. In keeping with the author's intent, yes. But ultimately not official - if it was, Rose could easily just add it to the FAQ, but she hasn't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-06T10:12:12-08:00","id":1044586,"title":"","content":"The book it is in has sections for mage, vampire, werewolf, etc correct. If it is listed in that section the it is as good as in the vampire books, that section was written with vampire in mind. I personally don't own the book at this time it is next on the purchase list.<br /> <br /> I am just saying that real world physics that they are arguing about hold little weight in a fantacy setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12802,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","user":"Hardwire99","date":". 02-06-2017, 01:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-06T15:26:53-08:00","id":1044746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1042925-lightning-vs-vampires?p=1044517#post1044517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you reference where it is said that Vampires can't have Pyrokinesis?</div> </div> </div> </div>3rd paragraph on pg200 Secrets of the Covenants - Coil of Zirnitra:<br /> <i>It's worth noting that this can cause unintended complications for a chronicle. Not every human Supernatural Merit will work well within a Vampire chronicle. Use firm discretion, and discuss each purchase with your storyteller.</i><br /> <br /> Also, electricity is not inherently any more damaging to dead matter than say a gunshot. Yes electricity can burn and even vaporize flesh catastrophically, but it's no any more devastating than having flesh burned and vaporized by a high velocity rifle bullet.<br /> Arguments that specifically lightning is somehow different from regular electricity are also flawed because it's actually the same comparison as being shot by .38 special vs a 30-06. It's just a bigger, badder version of the same concept.<br /> <br /> I'm fine it working &quot;because he spent XP&quot;, but not &quot;because it's lightning&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11661,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","user":"Rathamus","date":". 02-06-2017, 06:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-06T20:40:34-08:00","id":1044864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As with anything, you have to consider its impact in your game. Adding a pyrokinetic character to your Vampire: The Requiem game might be a little difficult. Then again, it might be awesome. </div> </div> </div>As a natural English reader, I say that means you can do what you want but pyrokinetic vampires are not advised. That is what I was saying by &quot;shouldn't.&quot; A pyrokinetic vampire <i>might</i> be possible. We won't be seeing any pyrokinetic vampire sample characters. It is the official word and I imagine people get tired of writing the same damn disclaimer the same way all the time so I am understanding of using literary device even though it may have confused intent. It is what it is. If you think because vampires controlling fire makes no sense and don't allow them, the rules are with you. If you don't care and want pyrokinetic vampires anyway, the rules are with you also. I wanted to point that out because there was some indication of a belief that there was ambiguity. Ambivalence might be accurate, not ambiguity.<br /> <br /> People are talking across each other about the electricity thing. There is ambiguity in this case. There is no indication whether the attack would be similar to a lightning attack or an electric shock attack. Lightning is plasma so it burns. Lightning is caused by electricity which flows with the plasma. I could see lightning doing bashing damage because that would be more like a bullet. Electric shock would be more like a heat ray or microwaves. It would not be isolated to a small area like a gunshot so there is room to consider it as lethal damage, like getting hit by a truck at high speed. A vampire would be less affected in the sense that it would get up afterwards but the vampire's body would be a wreck.<br /> <br /> I don't know which to go with but if someone can control electricity and how it flows then they could at range force an electric shock. Normally, lightning never strikes a person. Near strikes are survivable and would cause burns. Lightning striking <i>through</i> a person would be a lethal electric shock. Nobody could walk away from that. We are talking electric chair horror stories where people actually burst into flames only there would be no hyperbole. I doubt the merit has that much juice but it could be the same effect on a smaller scale. Maybe the effect is extensive enough to still be lethal, or not.<br /> <br /> I don't think everyone agrees in the form the damage takes. There is no point in going back and forth when a different damage is being considered depending on the individual. Pick one or go around in circles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T02:58:42-08:00","id":1044971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1042925-lightning-vs-vampires?p=1044864#post1044864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think everyone agrees in the form the damage takes. There is no point in going back and forth when a different damage is being considered depending on the individual. Pick one or go around in circles.</div> </div> </div> </div> I don't think that anyone is disagreeing over the form that damage takes. Or, rather, they're all happy with anyone ruling whatever way. If someone wants to say &quot;you invested XP into a power that will deal lethal to vampires&quot; and allow it? No one here seems to be really opposed to anyone ruling that way or the other. And it is an individual ST ruling in this case. Hell, anything and everything you take with Zirnitra is going to be an ST ruling at pretty much every step of the way. Which, by and by, is the ultimate answer to the OP's question - your ST made the ruling, and zie gets final say, there's no rule to argue against that.<br /> <br /> The problem that seems to be coming up is the justifications to allow lethal beyond the above. We're dealing with justifiactions that are inconsistant with the rules as printed. Is it so wrong to address that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T03:53:12-08:00","id":1044981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rathamus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1042925-lightning-vs-vampires?p=1044746#post1044746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 3rd paragraph on pg200 Secrets of the Covenants - Coil of Zirnitra:<br /> <i>It's worth noting that this can cause unintended complications for a chronicle. Not every human Supernatural Merit will work well within a Vampire chronicle. Use firm discretion, and discuss each purchase with your storyteller.</i><br /> <br /> ...</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm... And how does this translates to &quot;vampires can't have Pyrokinesis&quot;?<br /> <br /> That is basically what is in Hurt Locker, which is your basic &quot;make sure it is alright with the ST to purchase any of these powers&quot;.<br /> <br /> Still waiting for something like &quot;Vampires can't have powers which gives them control over their Banes&quot;. Or any outright statement on those notes. But I think I will wait a long time, because they don't exist.<br /> <br /> The other part of your post wasn't addressed to me I believe, and I have no coment on that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T04:11:27-08:00","id":1044986,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1042925-lightning-vs-vampires?p=1044864#post1044864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a natural English reader, I say that means you can do what you want but pyrokinetic vampires are not advised. That is what I was saying by &quot;shouldn't.&quot; A pyrokinetic vampire <i>might</i> be possible. We won't be seeing any pyrokinetic vampire sample characters. It is the official word and I imagine people get tired of writing the same damn disclaimer the same way all the time so I am understanding of using literary device even though it may have confused intent. It is what it is. If you think because vampires controlling fire makes no sense and don't allow them, the rules are with you. If you don't care and want pyrokinetic vampires anyway, the rules are with you also. I wanted to point that out because there was some indication of a belief that there was ambiguity. Ambivalence might be accurate, not ambiguity.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>If &quot;might be difficult, but could be awesome&quot; means &quot;advise against&quot; it just looks like antiquated parents advice to teen agers. It is hard (and could be fun), so don't do it! As a proficient English reader, I don't think that is the intent of the advice. The intent is pretty clear; might be difficult, but could be awesome. So go for it if you want to work through the difficulty and believe there is awesome to be found.<br /> <br /> There is no &quot;might&quot; to the possibility. Pyrokinetic vampires are possible, by the rules. They are as possible as vampire Mediums, Apporters, Lay on Handers, Amulet Blessers and Telepaths. <br /> <br /> Now, just because they are possible it doesn't mean they exist in every table. Which is fine. <br /> <br /> On the lightning thing I already said how I would handle. I just think the advice offered by the devs/writers is a slippery slope. People spend exp on a bunch of things, should they all cause lethal to vamps? A character sacrifices their Defense to make an all out attack, should they also do lethal to vamps?<br /> <br /> It is just fodder for shitty arguments at the table.<br /> <br /> Vampires downgrade most damage. Electricity, lightning or otherwise, is not cited as an exception, so it gets downgraded. That is how I would geerally rule.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T10:16:04-08:00","id":1045197,"title":"","content":"I agree. Electricity damages mortals because its interference with bioelectric signal (heart) and because high heat developed. Heat isn't fire. Some oven can be hotter than some kind of fire, but fire deal aggravates cause it is &quot;mystically&quot; a bane for vampire. As mystical as sunlight is. Sunlight is simply an electromagnetic field (with several frequencies) as the light of a light bulb is. UV doesn't damage vampire in requiem as far as I know. <br /> And in any case, if we consider high heat as a source of damage similar to fire it should deal aggravated damage, if not, it should be downgraded as all other sources to bashing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 02-07-2017, 02:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T18:11:31-08:00","id":1045536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1042925-lightning-vs-vampires?p=1044971#post1044971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I don't think that anyone is disagreeing over the form that damage takes. Or, rather, they're all happy with anyone ruling whatever way. If someone wants to say &quot;you invested XP into a power that will deal lethal to vampires&quot; and allow it? No one here seems to be really opposed to anyone ruling that way or the other. And it is an individual ST ruling in this case. Hell, anything and everything you take with Zirnitra is going to be an ST ruling at pretty much every step of the way. Which, by and by, is the ultimate answer to the OP's question - your ST made the ruling, and zie gets final say, there's no rule to argue against that.<br /> <br /> The problem that seems to be coming up is the justifications to allow lethal beyond the above. We're dealing with justifiactions that are inconsistant with the rules as printed. Is it so wrong to address that?</div> </div> </div> </div>It isn't wrong but the justifications are where the form of damage is being mixed. If people are thinking of different things when they start their justifying then it becomes apples and oranges. <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Lightning, high tension wires, house wiring are different situations. I'm seeing them in arguments as if they were the same which more likely means people have different things in mind when they start their justifications. </span></span></span>I think it probably just comes down to buying into the invested XP argument or saying pfft to that. As you say, then it comes down to personal preference.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T11:38:10-08:00","id":1045882,"title":"","content":"In the setting as we've developed it, vampires aren't supposed to be able to control banes. But if you want pyrokinetic vampires, I'm the last person who's going to try and stop you!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T04:16:08-08:00","id":1046242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1042925-lightning-vs-vampires?p=1045882#post1045882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the setting as we've developed it, vampires aren't supposed to be able to control banes. But if you want pyrokinetic vampires, I'm the last person who's going to try and stop you!</div> </div> </div> </div>Good thing the Ordo is all about vampires doing what vampires <i>aren\u00b4t supposed</i> to do then! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T06:39:50-08:00","id":1046285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1042925-lightning-vs-vampires?p=1046242#post1046242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Good thing the Ordo is all about vampires doing what vampires <i>aren\u00b4t supposed</i> to do then! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>+1 and Subscribed !. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}